        <p>LANCASHIRE &amp; CHESHIRE COUNTY NEWSPAPERS</p>
        <p>COMPRISES rr HE Warrington and Mid-Cheshire Examiner pub- 1 Behr d Saturday morning, The district covered by the Paper comprises many populous manufacturing towns and villages, and a la ge agricultural tract. THE Earlestown and Newton Examin6r,and Ashton, Golborne, and Haydock Reporter, published Friday afternoon. The district is in the heart of the Lancashire coal field. THE St. Helens Examtner and Preseot Weekly News, published Friday afternoon. The district ccmprises the centre of the Wass, Chemical, and Watch Trades of the King- dom. &amp;c. rrHE Runeor;t Examiner, published griday morn- ing. IL is the only Weekly Paper in the district, and offers the best and cheapest, facilities to advertisers. rr HE Widnes Examiner, published Friday morn- -1- ing. Widnes contains the largest number of Chemical Works of any town in the kingdom, and is rapidly becoming , an important centre of industry. Auction, Education, Wanted, To be Let, On Sale, Legal, Public Meeting, Sermon, Lecture, Bazaar, and other Public Notices, Advertisements (exct pt Parliamentary) are inserted in all the above papers at one charge. PREPAID ADVERTISEMENTS.</p>
