      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-10-20_WidnesExaminer_art0029" n="art0029">
        <head>NEWS OF THE GAME.</head>
        <p>NEWS OF THE GAME.</p>
        <p>St. Helens players will be pleased to hear that Mr. R. Atwell, a native of that town, has won the Championship of the London Wanderers Draughts Club. Mr.H.Jacob was the holder when Mr. Atwell challenged him,he having wonthe title in a tourna- ment. Mr. Atwell has now been challenged in turn by Mr. A. Jordan, the champion of London, which meeting is already looked forward to with the greatest of interest. We cannot but hope that the "Lancashire lad" will be able to retain the title which he has so meritoriously won.</p>
        <p>The small diagram will enable our readers to understand the notation by which the moves of the game are recorded. Black occupies the squares num- bered 1 to 12 and white those numbered 21 to 32. The figures thus 11-15 indicate that a move is made from and to the squares so numbered. Black has the opening move and the oaks of figures apply alternately to Black and White to the close.</p>
