        <p>NEW RATE FOR CLIFTON.</p>
        <p>A rate of ls. 31. in too £ vr49 ma ,ctioned before the Rai:worn mist at.s, on Tuosday, tor the tlwriship of Clifton. The ra'e is e-tinw ed to realise £255 1.1 4d.</p>
        <p>"SCHOLARS SUNDAY" AT RUNCORN.</p>
        <p>" Sarru4y" was ,observed at ths various chapels in connection with the Runcorn Wosieytn cir- cut on Sanity laic.. Tor m eting in connection with Sc. Paw's was held in the Brubsw.ck Schools, wider the presidency ot Mr. T. Simister. The scholars were ad- dressed by the Rev. 11. Morrison, and Mr. Pet.r Lawson, one of the t ,ach.rs. The -I,,akerl at other plac s were —Halton, Reg. C. W. L. Christien (suce•intendent min- ister) ; Mill Brow; Rev. J. A. B. Malvrrn ; and Ctmden, the principals of the teachins; staff.</p>
