      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-10-20_WidnesExaminer_art0065" n="art0065">
        <head>WIDNES CONiTABLE T) FIG IT THE BOERS,</head>
        <p>A WIDNES CONiTABLE T) FIG IT THE BOERS,</p>
        <p>r. C. Claroof the Linca.hire Co, stanulary, lett Widnes at noon on M oi,day en route for Ch Iset Brrrackq to joi his regimen., tiie Coldstrearns, who hive been callei out for special serv.;ce in the Transvaal. An interes!ing pre- sentation was m ,de to him by Superintendent K igntev, of the Widnes poic, force, of a pipe, a supply of tobacco and a purse of money. In a few words the recipient was wished G d—peied and a sate return. The money was sub:cribe i by his brother offic;rs, amongst whom he is highly esteemed.</p>
        <p>RUNCDRN FREE LIBRARY.</p>
        <p>Daring the month ot 8-ptember th-. library was open 21 days, and the issues were as follows :—Theology 13, philosopl” 5, science 64, history, &amp; , 75, poetry 12, fiction 1,512, miscellaneous 131, Friior:ll literature 4., n3u4ic 7, reference works 39, total 1,862 : being au in- crease iu the lending department of 857, and in the referenee'departm9lit of 16.</p>
